Package: orphacodes
Title: Rare Disease Nomenclature, Coding, Harmonisation and Registry
    Interoperability with 'Orphanet'
Version: 1.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "Imad",
      family = "El Badisy",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "elbadisyimad@gmail.com"
    )
  )
Description: A toolkit for managing rare disease data coded with the
    'Orphanet' nomenclature <https://www.orpha.net/>. It downloads and
    parses the 'Orphanet' nomenclature files for coding and the free
    'Orphadata' products into a versioned, cached database; validates and
    normalises ORPHAcodes; standardises free-text disease names to
    ORPHAcodes through preferred terms, synonyms and fuzzy matching;
    navigates the 'Orphanet' classifications and the linearisation
    (preferential parent); maps ORPHAcodes to and from ICD-10, ICD-11,
    OMIM, MONDO, UMLS, MeSH, MedDRA and GARD while preserving the
    direction, type and validation status of every alignment; tracks
    deprecated and obsolete codes with their replacements and compares
    two nomenclature releases; generates 'REDCap' data dictionaries and
    coding quality reports for rare disease registries; aggregates
    patient-level data at any level of the classification; and returns
    the 'Orphanet' epidemiological reference data for each code.
